e-s"],["Bar del Corso","dish/bar-del-corso"],["Barbetta","dish/barbetta"],["Barbuto (restaurant)","dish/barbuto-restaurant"],["Bella Italia","dish/bella-italia"],["Beppi's Restaurant","dish/beppi-s-restaurant"],["Bertucci's","dish/bertucci-s"],["BiCE Ristorante","dish/bice-ristorante"],["Biscotti","dish/biscotti"],["Black' Smith","dish/black-smith"],["Bocca di Lupo","dish/bocca-di-lupo"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Bombolone","dish/bombolone"],["Buca di Beppo","dish/buca-di-beppo"],["Budino","dish/budino"],["Buona","dish/buona"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Caffé Vittoria","dish/caffe-vittoria"],["Camille's (Providence, Rhode Island)","dish/camille-s-providence-rhode-island"],["Campisi's Egyptian Restaurant","dish/campisi-s-egyptian-restaurant"],["Cannelloni","dish/cannelloni"],["Capellini","dish/capellini"]]}]},"dish/peking-duck":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/peking-duck","n":"Peking duck","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Beijing cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Peking duck is a dish from Beijing that has been prepared since the Imperial era. The meat is characterized by its thin, crispy skin, with authentic versions of the dish serving mostly the skin and little meat, sliced in front of the diners by the cook. Ducks bred especially for the dish are slaughtered after 65 days and seasoned before being roasted in a closed or hung oven. The meat is often eaten with spring onion, cucumber, and sweet bean sauce, with pancakes rolled around the fillings. Aromatic duck is a similar dish to Peking duck and is popular in the United Kingdom and Ireland."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-peking-duck"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peking_duck"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Beijing cuisine","cuisine/beijing-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Allium fistulosum","ingredient/allium-fistulosum"],["Duck as food","ingredient/duck-as-food"],["Spring pancake","ingredient/spring-pancake"],["Tianmianjiang","ingredient/tianmianjiang"]]}]},"ingredient/siling-haba":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/siling-haba","n":"Siling haba","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 3 cuisines","intro":[["Siling haba (\"long chili\"), espada (\"sword\" in Spanish), siling mahaba, siling pangsigang (\"chili for sinigang\"), siling Tagalog (\"Tagalog chili\"), and sometimes called green chili, finger chili or long pepper, is one of two kinds of chili common to the Philippines and Filipino cuisine, the other being siling labuyo. Unlike siling labuyo, it belongs to the species Capsicum annuum."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-siling-haba"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siling_haba"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":3,"groups":[["Filipino cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine",[["Piyanggang manok","dish/piyanggang-manok"]]],["Mindanao cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-mindanao",[["Piyanggang manok","dish/piyanggang-manok"]]],["Visayan cuisine","cuisine/filipino-cuisine-visayas",[["Piyanggang manok","dish/piyanggang-manok"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Coconut milk","ingredient/coconut-milk"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Lemongrass","ingredient/lemongrass"],["Turmeric","ingredient/turmeric"]]}]},"dish/salmorejo":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/salmorejo","n":"Salmorejo","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Spanish cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Salmorejo, sometimes known as ardoria or ardorío, is a traditional soup originating from Córdoba, Andalusia, southern Spain, made of tomato, bread, extra virgin olive oil and garlic. The salmorejo is served cold and may be garnished with diced Spanish ibérico ham and diced hard-boiled eggs."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-salmorejo"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salmorejo"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Spanish cuisine","cuisine/spanish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Candeal bread","ingredient/candeal-bread"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Olive oil","ingredient/olive-oil"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Spain on a Fork","ref":"site/spainonafork-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"spainonafork.com","note":"Albert Bevia's video channel and site of traditional and everyday Spanish recipes.","url":"https://spainonafork.com/welcome2/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Spanish cuisine","links":[["Andrajos","dish/andrajos"],["Ataula","dish/ataula"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Buñuelo","dish/bunuelo"],["Caldo galego","dish/caldo-galego"],["Chistorra","dish/chistorra"],["Churro","dish/churro"],["Cocido","dish/cocido"],["Cuajada","dish/cuajada"],["El Quijote (restaurant)","dish/el-quijote-restaurant"],["El Willy","dish/el-willy"],["Embutido","dish/embutido"],["Esquina Común","dish/esquina-comun"],["Gazpacho","dish/gazpacho"],["Hojuela","dish/hojuela"],["Jamón","dish/jamon"],["Migas","dish/migas"],["Mojo (sauce)","dish/mojo-sauce"],["Ogasawara-Hakushaku-Tei","dish/ogasawara-hakushaku-tei"],["Patatas a lo pobre","dish/patatas-a-lo-pobre"],["Patatas bravas","dish/patatas-bravas"],["Picatostes","dish/picatostes"],["Pincho","dish/pincho"],["Pottage","dish/pottage"],["Salchichón","dish/salchichon"],["Sobrassada","dish/sobrassada"],["Soldaditos de Pavía","dish/soldaditos-de-pavia"],["Somni","dish/somni"],["Sopa de gato","dish/sopa-de-gato"],["Spanish omelette","dish/spanish-omelette"],["Spanish restaurant","dish/spanish-restaurant"],["Stuffed peppers","dish/stuffed-peppers"],["Tapas","dish/tapas"],["Toro Bravo (restaurant)","dish/toro-bravo-restaurant"],["Turrón","dish/turron"]]}]},"ingredient/hilsa":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/hilsa","n":"Hilsa","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The ilish (Tenualosa ilisha) (Bengali: ইলিশ, romanized: iliś), also known as the ilishi, hilsa, pulasa, hilsa herring or hilsa shad, is a species of fish related to the herring, in the family Clupeidae. It is a very popular and sought-after food in the Bengal region and area and is the national fish of Bangladesh. It is also the state fish of the Indian state of West Bengal."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-hilsa"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hilsa"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Bangladeshi cuisine","cuisine/bangladeshi-cuisine",[["Shorshe ilish","dish/shorshe-ilish"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Ilish","ingredient/ilish"],["Mustard","ingredient/mustard"],["Mustard (condiment)","ingredient/mustard-condiment"],["Mustard oil","ingredient/mustard-oil"],["Turmeric","ingredient/turmeric"]]}]},"dish/taix-restaurant":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/taix-restaurant","n":"Taix (restaurant)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Taix (formerly Les Freres Taix) was a French restaurant in Los Angeles, California, founded in 1927. The restaurant complex, located at 1911 Sunset Boulevard in the city's Echo Park neighborhood, featured open and private dining rooms, banquet halls, and a cocktail lounge with live music called the 321 Lounge. The restaurant closed on March 29, 2026, and is slated to re-open in 2029 following redevelopment of the property."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-taix-restaurant"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taix_(restaurant)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine"],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pardon Your French","ref":"site/pardonyourfrench-com","color":"#55